  {
    "type": "NarrativeText",
    "element_id": "e311d4d71b5991ac0ea23e9d105525f2",
    "text": "For \"BSBINN301 Supporting documentation.docx\", The document provides several activities and tools that can be used to agree and communicate responsibilities in ways that encourage team-based innovation. The 'Destroying assumptions guide' and the 'Manufacturing and quality control procedures' both outline processes where team members are assigned specific roles and responsibilities. These activities encourage team-based innovation by having members work together towards a common goal. However, the document does not explicitly state how to organize and agree on effective ways of working. The content is more focused on providing examples of team roles and responsibilities rather than the process of agreeing on them. Therefore, while the document partially meets the criterion, it does not fully satisfy all aspects of it.",
    "metadata": {
      "languages": [
        "eng"
      ],
      "filename": "17347.txt",
      "filetype": "text/plain",
      "parent_id": "88b60980693acfcfdc73e1473b8dfc2a",
      "data_source": {
