  {
    "type": "NarrativeText",
    "element_id": "311f8205e2ef8edbc1664857ddd1a588",
    "text": "# *Reference:* _\"Elect an Assumption Destruction Manager. The Assumption Destruction Manager calls a team together representing a cross-section of the organisation's human resources.\"_ *Section:* Destroying assumptions guide # *Reference:* _\"The possible job roles for this activity (if you wish to divide your team up into individual roles) are outlined below.\"_ *Section:* Manufacturing and quality control procedures # *Reference:* _\"Cutter: Cuts the paper according to paper design (has scissors).\"_ *Section:* Rules and roles # *Reference:* _\"Folder: Folds the paper according to the work instruction and outline of folds.\"_ *Section:* Rules and roles # *Reference:* _\"Tester: Tapes masking tape to the floor to designate throwing line, centre line and acceptable quality landing zone. The tester conducts three test flights to see if the plane can fly the 5 meter required distance and that it lands within the acceptable quality landing zone.\"_ *Section:* Rules and roles # *Reference:* _\"Quality Control Inspector: Marks acceptable and unacceptable aeroplanes and puts the acceptable planes in sandwich bags and the unacceptable planes in rework bin (has tape and ruler). The quality control inspector gives the acceptable planes to the production manager.\"_ *Section:* Rules and roles # *Reference:* _\"Production Manager:_",
    "metadata": {
